WEBVTT

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:56.823
Arusu, who has somehow arrived in
a magical world, just can't accept...

00:00:56.924 --> 00:01:00.258
...the witches' reason
for capturing fairies.

00:01:01.695 --> 00:01:06.531
Finding herself with nowhere to go,
Arusu encounters an ecoo fairy...

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:10.001
...and was able to get him
to grant her a wish...

00:01:10.938 --> 00:01:14.772
But in exchange for her wish, she loses
the precious book her father gave her...

00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:17.970
...the one that will help
her to become a magician.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:50.535
Tweeny Witches

00:02:55.109 --> 00:02:59.569
The Book of Spells

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:03.010
Big deal!

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:05.682
You stole it from
a magic library, right?

00:03:05.786 --> 00:03:08.619
Hang on a sec!
I would never do such a thing...

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:13.287
Hey, hold up. Could that book
be from this world, maybe?

00:03:13.627 --> 00:03:15.925
Arusu, are you seriously
questioning that?

00:03:15.996 --> 00:03:16.656
Huh?

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.000
That book is a bible
for apprentice witches.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:22.967
If it's not from our world,
then what world could it be from?

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.799
Hey, are you listening?

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.049
I'm going to go look for it.

00:03:26.073 --> 00:03:27.040
I'm going to go look for it.
Arusu!

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:29.502
What's up with her?

00:03:36.116 --> 00:03:38.517
Tell us... who is that girl?

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:41.347
No matter who she is,
I'm sure she doesn't have...

00:03:41.455 --> 00:03:43.583
...the book of spells anymore.

00:03:43.657 --> 00:03:44.818
What?

00:03:44.925 --> 00:03:48.418
If it was that important to her,
it would've vanished in exchange...

00:03:48.495 --> 00:03:51.465
...for having her wish granted
at the very same moment.

00:03:51.532 --> 00:03:53.660
Vanished? But where?

00:03:53.767 --> 00:03:57.203
Who knows?
That's one thing we'll never find out.

00:03:57.304 --> 00:04:02.037
Why was it my bad luck to grant
children their troublesome wishes?

00:04:02.142 --> 00:04:05.407
| often ask myself why, and
it's just as much of a mystery!

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:06.240
Humph.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.888
Sheila! Eva!

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:17.582
It's morning! Wake up!
It's really nice outside!

00:04:17.691 --> 00:04:19.455
I'm still so sleepy.

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:23.162
What do you mean nice outside?

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:28.029
I'm going home after breakfast, okay?

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:33.439
This is a cool magical world, but
| bet Yoko really misses me by now.

00:04:33.841 --> 00:04:34.933
Yoko?

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.576
My mother.

00:04:37.978 --> 00:04:41.937
She's a real piece of work and
can't do a thing without my help.

00:04:42.149 --> 00:04:44.243
Go home? But how?

00:04:44.351 --> 00:04:47.446
Oh, what was her name? That old lady,
Ate-something-or-other?

00:04:47.554 --> 00:04:48.487
You mean Atelia?

00:04:48.555 --> 00:04:51.855
Right, that one. I'll just have a
heart-to-heart with that old lady.

00:04:52.092 --> 00:04:55.995
She looks like a big shot.
Maybe she knows a way to get me home.

00:04:56.864 --> 00:04:58.798
And hey, don't worry.

00:04:58.932 --> 00:05:02.596
I'll be sure to tell her you guys
didn't know I was human.

00:05:02.703 --> 00:05:06.071
Just a minute. She's never
gonna buy that kind of story...

00:05:07.641 --> 00:05:08.540
You...

00:05:08.742 --> 00:05:09.886
Thanks for breakfast!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.309
Thanks for breakfast!
Arusu...

00:05:12.946 --> 00:05:16.712
| couldn't fly yesterday...
even though I got on the broom.

00:05:18.218 --> 00:05:22.018
Maybe that means humans should just
stay in the Human Realm after all.

00:05:22.122 --> 00:05:22.987
Arusu!

00:05:24.725 --> 00:05:27.660
You should've just stayed
put from the start.

00:05:36.904 --> 00:05:39.202
| hear you've lost the book of spells.

00:05:39.306 --> 00:05:39.795
Huh?

00:05:40.774 --> 00:05:44.677
Well, I guess you already
know everything then!

00:05:45.312 --> 00:05:47.280
Even the fact that I'm human.

00:05:47.381 --> 00:05:49.213
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:05:49.316 --> 00:05:51.194
Where did you get that book of spells?

00:05:51.218 --> 00:05:52.151
Where did you get that book of spells?
Excuse me?

00:05:52.252 --> 00:05:55.244
You mean why did my dad
have that book of spells!

00:05:55.522 --> 00:05:56.250
Dad?

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.151
You mean your dad, Arusu?

00:05:58.258 --> 00:06:01.990
Uh-huh. It was my fifth birthday, see...
Dad gave that book to me.

00:06:02.596 --> 00:06:03.825
Pretty wack, huh?

00:06:03.931 --> 00:06:07.925
I mean, it's a bible to teach
apprentice witches about magic, right?

00:06:08.035 --> 00:06:11.903
So why would my dad have a book
that should only be in this world?

00:06:12.005 --> 00:06:14.838
It doesn't make any sense.
I'm a human!

00:06:15.609 --> 00:06:20.012
That book isn't merely a bible for
apprentice witches to learn from.

00:06:21.982 --> 00:06:25.043
It is the book that has been
passed down through the ages...

00:06:25.152 --> 00:06:28.452
...the only one of its kind. Without
question, it is the True Book of Spells.

00:06:28.522 --> 00:06:31.548
A book with such terrible power...
And this girl had it?

00:06:31.725 --> 00:06:33.853
The book of spells
was stolen more than...

00:06:33.961 --> 00:06:36.623
...10 years ago and
has never been recovered.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:40.963
So you're saying that
it was my dad who stole it?

00:06:41.301 --> 00:06:44.601
Okay, then how did my dad
get to this world?

00:06:44.938 --> 00:06:47.600
And then how did he get back
to the Human Realm?

00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:50.871
This man you speak of... your father.

00:06:50.978 --> 00:06:52.742
Where is he now?

00:06:53.013 --> 00:06:54.071
I don't know.

00:06:54.214 --> 00:06:57.479
He left when I was little
and never came back.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:07:01.019
If there is some way to get back to
the Human Realm, I want you to tell me!

00:07:01.088 --> 00:07:04.683
The fact that you were able to
come here and use magic...

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:07.886
...must have something to do
with that book's power.

00:07:08.095 --> 00:07:11.497
You mean without the book,
there's nothing we can do?

00:07:11.598 --> 00:07:14.363
Are you saying it's impossible
for me to use magic...

00:07:14.468 --> 00:07:17.130
...or go back home
unless I have that book?

00:07:17.838 --> 00:07:19.315
No, that can't be true.

00:07:19.339 --> 00:07:19.999
No, that can't be true.
Huh?

00:07:20.741 --> 00:07:23.938
Arusu, you said so yourself...
Anyone can use magic...

00:07:24.044 --> 00:07:26.308
...if they believe with all their heart!

00:07:26.413 --> 00:07:29.212
It's gonna be okay.
I know you'll be able to use magic!

00:07:29.316 --> 00:07:31.284
Okay? So let's live together!

00:07:31.351 --> 00:07:33.376
Let's study magic together!

00:07:33.487 --> 00:07:34.318
Eva...

00:07:34.488 --> 00:07:35.546
Hold on.

00:07:35.689 --> 00:07:38.852
This one's gonna interfere
with our fairy capturing.

00:07:38.959 --> 00:07:40.603
How can we live with someone like...

00:07:40.627 --> 00:07:41.924
How can we live with someone like...
Wait.

00:07:50.337 --> 00:07:53.602
| used these myself
when I was an apprentice witch.

00:07:55.375 --> 00:07:58.276
| will make an exception
and allow you to live here.

00:07:58.345 --> 00:07:59.540
Atelia!

00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:02.748
But we must hide the fact
that this girl is human.

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:05.614
It's a secret between us.

00:08:05.719 --> 00:08:08.347
Even the grand master
must never find out.

00:08:08.455 --> 00:08:10.719
Oh, yay! Isn't this great, Arusu?

00:08:10.824 --> 00:08:11.950
Yeah.

00:08:12.526 --> 00:08:14.961
Why are you going so far to help her?

00:08:15.028 --> 00:08:17.360
I'm entrusting her to you, Sheila.

00:08:17.464 --> 00:08:18.727
Atelia...

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:25.029
Starting today, a new member
of the chick class will be...

00:08:25.105 --> 00:08:26.382
...training in magic with us...

00:08:26.406 --> 00:08:28.135
...training in magic with us...
Yoo-hoo! I'm Arusu!

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:30.938
<i>Nice to meet you! Woo hoo! Dazzle!</i>

00:08:31.978 --> 00:08:34.470
Arusu!

00:08:35.715 --> 00:08:36.546
Shut up!

00:08:38.585 --> 00:08:41.680
Jeez, don't tell me
you're the teacher, Sheila?

00:08:42.556 --> 00:08:44.615
I'm the discipline officer.

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:46.249
Just sit yourself down!

00:08:46.693 --> 00:08:48.889
Man, you're on a power trip.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.800
All right, turn to page 256
in the book of spells.

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:55.630
We're gonna start by
reviewing the fireball spell.

00:08:56.203 --> 00:08:59.571
For the fireball spell, we'll be using
fur from this ignis fairy.

00:09:01.508 --> 00:09:02.018
Hey, you!

00:09:02.042 --> 00:09:02.718
Hey, you!
They're gonna realize that you're human.

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.767
They're gonna realize that you're human.

00:09:04.845 --> 00:09:05.869
But...

00:09:06.113 --> 00:09:09.208
<i>Alpha kaben thegan de iota!</i>

00:09:12.452 --> 00:09:13.977
Now you give it a shot.

00:09:21.695 --> 00:09:24.756
<i>Alpha kaben thegan de iota!</i>

00:09:25.832 --> 00:09:26.663
Iotal

00:09:29.202 --> 00:09:30.670
Aren't you going to try?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.135
Sure, I am.

00:09:33.273 --> 00:09:35.469
Oh no, my hand slipped!

00:09:35.542 --> 00:09:36.703
What are you doing?

00:09:36.843 --> 00:09:38.242
Help!

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:42.173
Melissa said she was going to
show us the biggest flame...

00:09:42.282 --> 00:09:44.410
...and cast the fireball spell
on that rock.

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:51.851
| just showed you the
fire-extinguishing spell last week.

00:09:52.993 --> 00:09:55.758
But I can'tdo it!

00:09:56.563 --> 00:09:59.828
Hey! Can't anyone here
cast a water spell?

00:10:01.268 --> 00:10:02.360
Don't you dare butt in.

00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:04.802
And you call yourself a teacher?

00:10:04.938 --> 00:10:08.397
You are responsible for your own magic.
You've got to be self-reliant.

00:10:08.475 --> 00:10:09.738
That's what magic is all about.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.535
I can't put it out!

00:10:12.179 --> 00:10:13.738
What kind of person are you?

00:10:24.291 --> 00:10:27.386
Listen, fires can be put out
without using magic!

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.861
Don't just stand there staring!
Help her!

00:10:38.071 --> 00:10:39.095
Are you okay?

00:10:39.206 --> 00:10:40.139
Come on!

00:10:41.374 --> 00:10:42.808
Hot! Hot!

00:10:43.743 --> 00:10:45.643
Now you've gone and spoiled her.

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:46.405
Huh?

00:10:46.947 --> 00:10:50.212
She might have figured out how to
cast the fire-extinguishing spell.

00:10:50.317 --> 00:10:52.615
And if she died trying,
what would be the point?

00:10:52.686 --> 00:10:53.796
If it happens, it happens.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.845
If it happens, it happens.
Do you know what you're saying?

00:10:55.956 --> 00:10:57.014
| already told you.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.116
In this world, the value of your life is
determined by how well you can use magic.

00:11:00.193 --> 00:11:02.685
The only big shots here are
the ones with magical skills!

00:11:02.762 --> 00:11:05.163
Those who can't use magic are
doomed to lead unhappy lives.

00:11:05.265 --> 00:11:07.563
And if you can't protect yourself,
then it's only a...

00:11:07.634 --> 00:11:09.500
...matter of time
before you end up dead!

00:11:09.569 --> 00:11:11.264
What kind of nonsense is that?

00:11:11.371 --> 00:11:13.635
Why don't you help each other out
when you have magic?

00:11:13.707 --> 00:11:14.572
Arusu!

00:11:16.376 --> 00:11:19.073
If that's how it is,
I'm gonna change things!

00:11:19.479 --> 00:11:23.438
I'm gonna go all out and learn this
magic stuff, and make everyone happy!

00:11:33.059 --> 00:11:36.051
Tweeny Witches

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:45.060
The Gryphon's Feather

00:11:48.575 --> 00:11:52.102
So you're gonna go all out and learn
magic, and make everyone happy?

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:54.470
Look, what you're saying
is contradictory!

00:11:54.581 --> 00:11:55.605
Contradictory?

00:11:56.049 --> 00:11:59.144
You were totally against us
catching fairies, right?

00:11:59.219 --> 00:12:02.382
That's right. Taking away a living
creature's freedom is the worst...

00:12:02.455 --> 00:12:04.822
But if you don't take away
the fairies' freedom...

00:12:04.891 --> 00:12:06.791
...there's no way magic can happen.

00:12:06.893 --> 00:12:08.486
Huh? What do you mean?

00:12:08.595 --> 00:12:09.338
Go on, tell her.

00:12:09.362 --> 00:12:10.124
Go on, tell her.
Uh, okay.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:13.097
Um... Arusu, it means
that along with mantras...

00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:16.601
...we need a fairy's body parts
to cast magical spells.

00:12:16.703 --> 00:12:20.367
Oh, I kinda remember
you mentioning something like that...

00:12:20.807 --> 00:12:23.469
For example, you know the spell
that lets you fly on a broom?

00:12:23.543 --> 00:12:24.374
Oh, yeah!

00:12:24.477 --> 00:12:26.969
That's the one
| wanted to learn today...

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.807
For that to work, you need a feather
from a fairy called a gryphon.

00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:32.476
A gryphon's feather?

00:12:32.585 --> 00:12:34.519
Before you can fly up
in the sky on a broom...

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:38.421
...you've got to catch a gryphon
and pluck one of its feathers first.

00:12:38.525 --> 00:12:39.458
What?

00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:41.924
And yet here you are saying
idealistic things like...

00:12:41.995 --> 00:12:44.054
...we shouldn't take away
a fairy's freedom.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.258
That's what I mean by contradictory!

00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:49.827
We witches have always upheld
our magical traditions...

00:12:49.903 --> 00:12:51.928
...through the sacrifice of fairies.

00:12:52.005 --> 00:12:55.168
We'll get you a lovely feather
as a present, Arusu.

00:12:55.241 --> 00:12:57.835
Huh? But I can't let you do that!

00:12:57.977 --> 00:12:59.502
Quid pro quo? A deal?

00:12:59.579 --> 00:13:01.673
Let's make a deal...
The price is right?

00:13:02.649 --> 00:13:04.708
Whatever, just shut the hell up.

00:13:05.085 --> 00:13:05.881
Sheila!

00:13:06.152 --> 00:13:08.086
| see one! I see a gryphon!

00:13:08.888 --> 00:13:11.789
Okay. We're gonna capture it
and regain our honor!

00:13:13.426 --> 00:13:16.191
What's that? That's just so uncool.

00:13:17.197 --> 00:13:19.291
It's the biker pilots, Sheila!

00:13:19.933 --> 00:13:21.958
Damn those dropout losers!

00:13:24.204 --> 00:13:26.730
What do you think you're doing?

00:13:27.974 --> 00:13:29.652
Don't interfere with our capture!

00:13:29.676 --> 00:13:30.302
Don't interfere with our capture!
Huh?

00:13:30.744 --> 00:13:32.007
What did you say?

00:13:32.078 --> 00:13:34.479
| can't hear you at all.

00:13:35.048 --> 00:13:36.140
Damn you...

00:13:36.883 --> 00:13:39.215
I'm warning you as discipline officer...

00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:43.085
I'm forbidding you to fly under
any circumstance in district A!

00:13:43.189 --> 00:13:45.920
Hey, hold up! The sky belongs to us all.

00:13:46.025 --> 00:13:48.687
People who disrupt this airspace
have no right to fly.

00:13:48.762 --> 00:13:49.695
Not cool!

00:13:49.763 --> 00:13:52.255
We're against all forms
of despotic government!

00:13:52.365 --> 00:13:53.628
It's not negotiable!

00:13:53.733 --> 00:13:56.532
If I catch you here again,
I'll report you to Atelia immediately!

00:13:56.603 --> 00:13:57.798
Keep that in mind!

00:14:05.211 --> 00:14:09.239
Come on, Sheila, for heaven's sake.
And you call yourself a witch?

00:14:09.449 --> 00:14:10.007
Huh?

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:13.848
I told you the measure of a witch
is how much she smiles...

00:14:13.953 --> 00:14:16.149
How happy she makes other people.

00:14:16.256 --> 00:14:20.124
Don't tell me you can't do anything
but act like the north wind!

00:14:20.226 --> 00:14:21.057
North wind?

00:14:21.161 --> 00:14:22.458
You know...

00:14:22.562 --> 00:14:24.462
It's just like that lame bunch said...

00:14:24.531 --> 00:14:26.499
...the sky belongs to
everyone, doesn't it?

00:14:26.599 --> 00:14:29.000
But what do you do? Forbid them to fly?

00:14:29.102 --> 00:14:31.264
Who ever gave you that kind of right?

00:14:31.504 --> 00:14:34.701
You can be so naive about this
because you don't know anything.

00:14:34.808 --> 00:14:35.468
Huh?

00:14:36.075 --> 00:14:36.837
Listen...

00:14:37.043 --> 00:14:40.274
Those guys are just dropouts who
make other people's lives miserable.

00:14:40.747 --> 00:14:43.876
If I don't crack down on them, they
just cause trouble for the rest of us.

00:14:43.983 --> 00:14:44.779
So...

00:14:45.151 --> 00:14:47.745
...if that's the case, there's got
to be a better way to handle it!

00:14:47.854 --> 00:14:50.448
Just shut up. This is my way
of handling it. Don't butt in!

00:14:50.557 --> 00:14:52.616
Hey! Come on, Sheila!

00:14:52.725 --> 00:14:56.389
Arusu, this is something
we just can't do anything about.

00:15:02.969 --> 00:15:05.734
Sheila! Something terrible's happened!

00:15:05.839 --> 00:15:07.864
That moron again? What did she do now?

00:15:07.941 --> 00:15:10.967
Arusu's joined the biker pilots!

00:15:11.077 --> 00:15:11.566
Huh?

00:15:15.548 --> 00:15:16.674
Go! Go!

00:15:17.183 --> 00:15:18.912
She can't even fly on her own...

00:15:19.085 --> 00:15:19.962
What are we gonna do?

00:15:19.986 --> 00:15:20.714
What are we gonna do?
Leave her alone.

00:15:20.787 --> 00:15:21.447
But...

00:15:21.588 --> 00:15:24.455
That just goes to show you
how serious she really was.

00:15:24.557 --> 00:15:25.956
I'm reporting this to Atelia.

00:15:26.059 --> 00:15:28.153
Wait, Sheila. Those people...

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:33.062
They might have come
to catch the gryphon.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.899
Let's go.

00:15:38.471 --> 00:15:41.338
It sure feels amazing,
flying freely in the sky.

00:15:41.441 --> 00:15:42.101
Doesn't it?

00:15:42.175 --> 00:15:47.170
Yeah, but you must be one hopeless
loser if you can't even fly.

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:50.807
Hey, I'd love to be able to fly,
but the, um... gryphon, was it?

00:15:50.917 --> 00:15:53.511
| bet that fairy wants to
fly freely in the sky himself.

00:15:53.586 --> 00:15:55.850
Just the thought of that
makes me not want to fly...

00:15:55.922 --> 00:15:58.186
...if it means I have
to capture it and all.

00:15:58.291 --> 00:16:00.191
Right... You're right!

00:16:00.293 --> 00:16:00.851
Huh?

00:16:01.227 --> 00:16:03.491
When they first gave us our feathers...

00:16:03.563 --> 00:16:06.362
...we had no idea that a fairy's
freedom had been taken away...

00:16:06.432 --> 00:16:08.400
...just so it could be plucked for us.

00:16:08.501 --> 00:16:11.869
But once we found out about that,
we started wondering whether...

00:16:11.938 --> 00:16:14.600
...it was really worth going
so far just to use magic.

00:16:14.674 --> 00:16:17.837
| mean, who wants to have
their freedom taken away, right?

00:16:17.944 --> 00:16:18.775
Right...

00:16:19.078 --> 00:16:23.106
That's why we never made it
past that first flying spell.

00:16:23.716 --> 00:16:25.115
And before we knew it...

00:16:25.184 --> 00:16:27.710
...everyone started calling us
flunkers and dropouts.

00:16:27.787 --> 00:16:28.982
| see.

00:16:30.089 --> 00:16:32.581
And that damned Sheila...

00:16:32.692 --> 00:16:35.923
| agree that wasn't the
best way to handle it, but...

00:16:36.029 --> 00:16:39.294
...the thing is, Sheila's got
something to protect too.

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:40.990
She's got to save face.

00:16:41.401 --> 00:16:43.995
Whose side are you on anyway?

00:16:45.071 --> 00:16:48.507
Everyone's side!
Because I'm an ally of justice!

00:16:48.775 --> 00:16:51.244
You really are an oddball.

00:16:52.845 --> 00:16:56.281
All right, troops!
Let's take to the skies one more time!

00:16:59.185 --> 00:17:02.450
You know, when you think about it,
the fairies... oops...

00:17:02.655 --> 00:17:04.521
Does it matter who captures them?

00:17:04.591 --> 00:17:05.990
Don't be ridiculous.

00:17:09.562 --> 00:17:11.052
Sheila, look!

00:17:15.301 --> 00:17:17.531
We found you, gryphon fairy.

00:17:20.373 --> 00:17:22.239
That's not gonna work!

00:17:22.342 --> 00:17:24.709
Hey, all we need are its
feathers anyway, right?

00:17:24.811 --> 00:17:27.337
Come on, let's grill the thing
and have it for lunch!

00:17:27.447 --> 00:17:31.077
Your only goal should be to capture it.
You'd better not treat it harshly!

00:17:31.184 --> 00:17:34.677
What should we do? A couple of
annoying twerps just appeared.

00:17:34.787 --> 00:17:36.118
Just ignore them.

00:17:36.222 --> 00:17:39.783
This is our way of doing things.
Just keep your mouths shut!

00:17:39.859 --> 00:17:42.226
Then we'll just have to
butt in physically!

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:46.225
Out of the way... Out of the way...

00:17:46.466 --> 00:17:48.298
| said get out of the way!

00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:50.096
You little pain in the butt!

00:17:51.838 --> 00:17:53.567
How dare you!

00:17:54.641 --> 00:17:55.938
Gotcha!

00:17:56.242 --> 00:17:57.175
Bullseye!

00:17:57.343 --> 00:17:57.935
Sheila!

00:18:00.246 --> 00:18:01.509
Sheila!

00:18:05.518 --> 00:18:06.451
Damn you!

00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:07.663
Getting in our way again?

00:18:07.687 --> 00:18:09.052
Getting in our way again?
Go! Go! Go!

00:18:09.255 --> 00:18:11.917
Come on, troops,
let's make a run for it!

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:15.323
You're in my way.

00:18:15.528 --> 00:18:17.326
Buzz off for God's sake!

00:18:26.973 --> 00:18:28.441
Let go of me!

00:18:28.541 --> 00:18:31.101
The last thing I want is your help!
Let go of me!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.871
Sorry, not gonna happen.

00:18:32.979 --> 00:18:35.710
Not as long as you have
the gryphon fairy.

00:18:35.815 --> 00:18:37.442
Don't tell me you're...

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.678
Okay, then I won't tell you!

00:18:40.486 --> 00:18:42.181
Go on, fly away!

00:18:43.222 --> 00:18:43.848
No!

00:18:53.299 --> 00:18:55.859
What do you mean you're gonna make
everyone happy with your magic?

00:18:55.935 --> 00:18:56.458
Huh?

00:18:56.803 --> 00:18:59.101
Nothing but garbage comes
out of that mouth of yours!

00:18:59.205 --> 00:19:03.108
Everything you do is the complete
opposite of learning magic!

00:19:03.209 --> 00:19:06.144
Hey, but one of these days,
I'll figure out a better way.

00:19:06.212 --> 00:19:10.547
A way to use magic without
taking away the fairies' freedom...

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.651
See, all you talk about is
stuff that's never gonna happen.

00:19:13.753 --> 00:19:14.797
Arusu!

00:19:14.821 --> 00:19:15.310
Arusu!
Yeah?

00:19:15.388 --> 00:19:18.050
Oh my gosh! How wonderful!
What a big surprise!

00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:20.219
Look! See?

00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:23.090
But why?

00:19:23.396 --> 00:19:27.731
I'm sure the gryphon fairy left it for you...
To thank you for saving it.

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.098
No way...
I've never heard of such a thing.

00:19:30.203 --> 00:19:32.763
But this is a gryphon's feather, right?

00:19:32.872 --> 00:19:33.682
It's a feather, right?

00:19:33.706 --> 00:19:34.832
It's a feather, right?
Well, well...

00:19:34.941 --> 00:19:37.774
| guess this means my way can work too.

00:19:40.346 --> 00:19:42.110
Hey, gryphon!

00:19:42.315 --> 00:19:44.044
You're the best!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:45.709
You're lovely!

00:19:49.555 --> 00:19:53.355
She has a point. I think her way
could work just as well.

00:19:53.826 --> 00:19:57.160
That moron!
Learning a funky way of flying...

00:19:58.898 --> 00:20:03.096
| don't want to fly with you!

00:20:03.402 --> 00:20:05.871
This broom is the best!

00:20:05.972 --> 00:20:07.599
Gryphons are the best!

00:20:07.673 --> 00:20:10.643
Freedom is the best!

00:20:16.983 --> 00:20:24.947
Come on, let's go!
Without closing our eyes...

00:20:25.191 --> 00:20:33.191
Our singing and laughter
fill the vast sky.

00:20:34.367 --> 00:20:42.367
We're headed for
our greatest longings.

00:20:43.609 --> 00:20:49.173
There's no wish
that can't come true.

00:20:49.282 --> 00:20:53.515
Let's just believe and fly away!

00:20:54.287 --> 00:20:58.520
No matter how hopeless it seems...
If we wish hard enough...

00:20:58.624 --> 00:21:03.186
See, it'll turn info magic.

00:21:03.396 --> 00:21:08.562
Even the tiniest dream...
If it can bring somebody joy...

00:21:08.668 --> 00:21:11.729
Let's hope it does.

00:21:13.206 --> 00:21:17.837
Hey! DuDiDuWa...
We're laughing always, lalala...

00:21:17.944 --> 00:21:20.436
Let's sing your song and
smile and laugh with me.

00:21:20.546 --> 00:21:28.546
The truth is we're all waiting...

00:21:29.722 --> 00:21:35.456
...for the world of our dreams.

00:21:35.561 --> 00:21:39.725
So we might as well
Just make one of our own!
